---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro'
import { LINKS, SITE } from '../../consts'

/*
 * Obligations page.
 *
 * The FFmpeg and TMDB notices below are required, not decorative. FFmpeg's
 * compliance checklist names websites explicitly; TMDB's API terms specify the
 * notice wording verbatim. Do not paraphrase either.
 */
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Licences & attribution"
  description="Licensing for Streamarr and Playarr, the FFmpeg and TMDB notices the project is required to display, and its trademark and patent position."
>
  <Section eyebrow="Legal" title="Licences and attribution">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="streamarr">Streamarr and Playarr</h2>
      <p>
        Streamarr's and Playarr's own source code is released under the MIT licence.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        <p>Copyright (c) 2026 Thomas McFarlane</p>
        <p>
          Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this
          software and associated documentation files (the “Software”), to deal in the Software
          without restriction, including without limitation the rights to use, copy, modify, merge,
          publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit
          persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:
        </p>
        <p>
          The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all copies or
          substantial portions of the Software.
        </p>
        <p>
          THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED “AS IS”, WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
          INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR
          PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE
          FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR
          OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER
          DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        The full text is in the <a href={LINKS.licence} rel="noopener">repository</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="ffmpeg">FFmpeg</h2>
      <p>
        This is an important distinction and worth stating plainly: <strong>{SITE.name}'s own
        source is MIT-licensed, but the published container images additionally bundle FFmpeg,
        which is licensed under the GNU General Public Licence version 2 or later.</strong> The
        image as a whole is therefore distributed subject to that licence.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        <p>
          This software uses libraries from the FFmpeg project under the GNU General Public Licence
          version 2 or later. FFmpeg is a trademark of Fabrice Bellard, originator of the FFmpeg
          project. {SITE.name} is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or the owner of FFmpeg.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        FFmpeg runs on the server as a separate process. It is <strong>not</strong> embedded in any
        Playarr client application.
      </p>
      <p class="todo">
        <strong>Corresponding source.</strong> Anyone distributing a Streamarr container image must
        make the exact corresponding FFmpeg source, and the build configuration used, available
        alongside the binaries. This page is where those links belong, per published image tag.
        They are not yet published here — if you need them before they are, please
        <a href={LINKS.issues} rel="noopener">open an issue</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="tmdb">TMDB</h2>
      <blockquote>
        <p>
          This website uses TMDB and the TMDB APIs but is not endorsed, certified, or otherwise
          approved by TMDB.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        Metadata identifiers and artwork reaching a Streamarr installation may originate with TMDB,
        by way of the library-management tools it reads from. TMDB is not a partner, sponsor or
        endorser of this project.
      </p>

      <h2 id="patents">Codecs and patents</h2>
      <p>
        Media codecs may be covered by patents in some jurisdictions. Nothing on this site, and no
        licence granted by this project, conveys any patent rights. Deploying this software
        commercially, or distributing builds of it, may require a separate patent licence depending
        on where you are and what you are doing. No claim is made that operating Streamarr is
        royalty-free.
      </p>

      <h2 id="third-party">Other third-party software</h2>
      <p>
        Streamarr and Playarr are built on a large amount of open-source software across their Rust
        and TypeScript trees. A generated dependency and licence inventory belongs here and is not
        yet published; the dependency manifests in the
        <a href={LINKS.repo} rel="noopener">repository</a> are authoritative in the meantime.
      </p>

      <h2 id="trademarks">Trademarks and affiliation</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} and {SITE.clientName} are independent projects. They are not affiliated with,
        endorsed by, or sponsored by Sonarr, Radarr, Lidarr, Bazarr, Prowlarr, Readarr, Tdarr,
        Plex, Jellyfin, Emby, Apple, Google, LG, Samsung, Hisense, Roku, or TMDB. All trademarks
        are the property of their respective owners, and are used here only to describe
        interoperability.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: var(--width-prose);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    scroll-margin-top: 90px;
  }

  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  blockquote {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  blockquote p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .todo {
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
</style>
